## Implementation Details

The Analytics component is correctly configured in the root layout:

```typescript
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        {children}
        <Analytics />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

This implementation:
- Uses the framework-specific import for Next.js (`@vercel/analytics/next`)
- Places the Analytics component inside the body tag
- Will automatically track page views and web vitals once deployed to Vercel

## Next Steps

To complete the setup and start collecting analytics data:

1. **Enable Analytics in Vercel Dashboard**
   - Navigate to your project in Vercel
   - Go to the Analytics tab
   - Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics

2. **Deploy to Vercel**
   - Run `vercel deploy` or push to the connected Git branch
   - Analytics will begin tracking automatically after deployment

3. **Verify Tracking**
   - Check browser Network tab for `/_vercel/insights/*` requests
   - View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after deployment

## Notes

- The implementation is production-ready and requires no additional code changes
- Analytics tracking only activates on Vercel deployments, not in local development
- The analytics package is version 2.0.1, which is the latest stable release
- Lock file updated to ensure consistent dependency resolution across environments
